Employee Performance Dashboard

An interactive Power BI dashboard tracking employee quality and performance KPIs — built to monitor task sampling, defect rates, and error trends across supervisors and work locations.

Overview

This dashboard tracks quality-control performance at the employee level. It surfaces core KPIs (task volume, sampling coverage, defect rate, fatal error rate, and an overall quality score) and lets you break them down by employee, supervisor, work location, and date.

Tools Used
Power BI Desktop
Power Query (data loading & transformation)
DAX (calculated measures)
Data Modeling
Data Model

Core table: Quality Data, with fields including:

EMP Name, Supervisor, Work Location, Date
Total Task, Samples
Defects, Fatel Errors
Calculated measures: Sampling Percentage, Defect Percentage, Fatal Error Percentage, Quality Score
Dashboard Contents
KPI Cards: Total Tasks, Samples, Sampling %, Defects, Defect %, Fatal Errors, Fatal Error %
Gauge: Overall Quality Score against target
Scatter Chart: Quality Score by Employee — spot top and bottom performers at a glance
Line Chart: Quality Score trend over time
Donut Chart: Quality Score breakdown by Supervisor
Clustered Bar Chart: Sampling Percentage by Supervisor
Map: Quality Score by Work Location
Date Slicer: filter the entire dashboard by time period
File

Employee_Performance_Dashboard.pbix — open in Power BI Desktop to explore.

Key Insights
Identifies which employees and supervisors have the highest/lowest quality scores
Flags locations or teams with elevated defect or fatal error rates
Tracks whether sampling coverage is consistent enough to trust the quality metrics
Shows performance trends over time to catch drops early

